ivalry in the air here also  shanks asking marco a second time to  join his crew is hilarious you remember  that he did that before when he came to  talk to whitebeard about teach so no  wonder that teach is in this chapter as  well it also proves once again how  powerful and capable marco truly must be  everyone respects him and he has come  out of confrontations with all the  strongest people pretty much unharmed  and alive the admirals of marine fort  blackbeard big mom and kaido this man  truly is indestructible i would  personally put him in the same category  as ben beckman rayleigh or zorro who are  still not too far away in power to their  captains the wretched pirates then drop  marco off at sphinx island which i think  is actually really important because the  way that i read this chapter this  basically means that luffy and the straw  hats won't be going to sphinx island  after all as some people have speculated  i mean if that were the case i feel like  marco would have said something about  meeting again or something similar or  even sail with the straw hats right away  i mean that doesn't mean that sphinx  island is off the table completely as  the next island or that luffy will never  go there i mean i really hope they do  visit aces and whitebeard's grave but i  personally still hope and believe that  the straw heads are going to albaf next  and not law or kids i laid out all the  reasons for that in this video here so  check that out later if you're  interested because as much as i'd love  to speculate more about the straw hat's  next adventure we don't have time for  that right now we have to move on from  one of my top 5 favorite characters  marco to one of my top three characters  the dark king himself  silver's rayleigh i am so so happy that  we got him back in the story again way  sooner than i personally dare to hope i  gotta say this entire plot line that we  got on amazon lilly is so  so good like what not only do we get a  battle sequence we get one with some of  the coolest characters in the show  hancock who we haven't seen get serious  at all before this and blackbeard who  barely gets any screen time at all to  show off his ridiculously overpowered  devil fruit and of course kobe who let's  be real has grown a lot but is clearly  not quite yet on that level necessary to  make any real impact here but let's  start from the beginning we basically  get a continuation of the little  interlude we got during wano where kobe  was sailing towards amazon lilly in  order to capture boa hancock parallel to  the events of the raid there seemed to  have been a battle between the navy  fleet and the kuja tribe now usually  hancock and her warriors would probably  easily have overpowered the marine  troops here however they haven't come  alone we finally get the first glimpse  at the result of the ssg the special  science group and the weapons that they  created to replace both the pacifista  and the warlords the seraphim and holy  smokes oda sensei really didn't fool  around with their design here they are  absolutely terrifying asenav which  according to wikipedia literally means a  burning one is a type of celestial or  heavenly being in judaism islam and  christianity they're basically the  highest rank of angels with terrible  powers apparently their winged  appearance also has origins in ancient  egypt and so looking at oda sensei  seraphim this naming scheme makes a lot  of sense because they all look like  members of king's lunarian tribe with  white hair wings and dark skin they have  star-shaped pupils which any good anime  lover will know is the global sign that  someone is ridiculously powerful in case  you know bungo stray dogs there is a  child character as well with a star eye  called yumena kyusuku if i remember  correctly that has a pretty terrifying  power as well now clearly these new  humanoid weapons are a combination of  different types of research that we have  seen throughout the story ku